    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d64">

                <pb facs="0121" n="39" xml:id="pg39"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to Marshal Stalin </hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d64-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-01-22">22 January 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Number 178, Top Secret and Personal, from the President to Marshal Stalin.</p>
                <p>I have decided to not have any press representatives at <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Argonaut</hi> and to permit only a small group of
                    uniformed service photographers from the American Navy to take the pictures that
                    we will want.</p>
                <p>Prime Minister Churchill agrees.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d64-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Roosevelt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d64-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d64-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the United States Naval Attaché, Moscow, via Navy channels.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d64-f2" n="2" xml:id="d64-f2-content">
                <p> Stalin’s reply, dated January 23, as received by the President in translation,
                    included the statements, “I do not have any objections against your proposals”
                    and “The same reply I sent to the Prime Minister’s request” (Roosevelt
                    Papers).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
